{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/ofy9wn61","slideIndex":2,"text":"RQ1. Chapter 6 §6.3.4. The three tensors are sampling-only, G = 8, 200 problems per seed, not a training delta. Pooled ZVF is 0.1583. The residual after mean reward is r = +0.21, 95% CI [−0.31, +0.62], n = 17. ZVF measures group-relative advantage-signal starvation. Predictive validity was not established. KL, auxiliary losses and optimizer state may still affect updates. High ZVF is also what mastery looks like.\nThe n=23 table pools heterogeneous records and membership of simulation-projection rows is unresolved. It is not a separately established measured-only cohort. This is a descriptive association from that table, not validated predictive performance."}
