{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/fu1gfa1s","slideIndex":7,"text":"The cohort is not a random benchmark sample. Assistant review is not independent human validation. The witnesses reject certainty from eight parser-zero answers on this checkpoint. They are not a gradient, a training gain, or a controller result. Santana's first successful number came from an incorrect argument.\nFrozen event: after eight initial parser-zero answers, at least one of 24 fresh responses matches the reference under parser v2. Cohort: deterministic first 64 eligible questions. Wilson 95% interval 9.88–28.21% is descriptive, not a population recovery estimate. The assistant-reviewed three numerical witnesses are separate."}
